<html>
  <head>
    <style>
      body {
        font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
        background: #f5f5f5;
        margin: 0;
        padding: 20px;
      }
      .container {
        max-width: 600px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        background: #ffffff;
        border-radius: 12px;
        overflow: hidden;
      }
      .header {
        background: #0b2343;
        padding: 30px;
        text-align: center;
      }
      .header h1 {
        color: #ffffff;
        margin: 0;
        font-size: 22px;
      }
      .header p {
        color: #94a3b8;
        margin: 6px 0 0;
        font-size: 14px;
      }
      .body {
        padding: 30px;
      }
      .body p {
        color: #333;
        line-height: 1.6;
      }
      .panel {
        background: #fafbfc;
        border: 1px solid #e5e7eb;
        border-radius: 8px;
        padding: 16px 20px;
        margin: 20px 0;
      }
      .panel dt {
        color: #6b7280;
        font-size: 12px;
        text-transform: uppercase;
        letter-spacing: 0.4px;
        margin-top: 8px;
      }
      .panel dd {
        color: #111827;
        font-size: 15px;
        margin: 4px 0 0;
      }
      .button {
        display: inline-block;
        background: #0b2343;
        color: #ffffff !important;
        padding: 12px 22px;
        border-radius: 8px;
        text-decoration: none;
        font-weight: 600;
        margin-top: 8px;
      }
      .footnote {
        color: #6b7280;
        font-size: 12px;
        margin-top: 24px;
        line-height: 1.5;
      }
      .footer {
        background: #f3f4f6;
        padding: 18px;
        text-align: center;
        color: #6b7280;
        font-size: 12px;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <div class="container">
      <div class="header">
        <h1>Learner ready for level review</h1>
        <p>{{adminLooksLikeOrg}}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="body">
        <p>Hello,</p>

        <p>
          <strong>{{learnerName}}</strong> has met all five level-progression
          criteria at <strong>{{currentLevel}}</strong>.
          The Amber platform has flagged this learner as a candidate for level
          review — but no automatic level change has been made. You decide
          whether to confirm a promotion or hold the learner at the current
          level.
        </p>

        <div class="panel">
          <dl>
            <dt>Learner</dt>
            <dd>{{learnerName}}</dd>
            <dt>Current NQF level</dt>
            <dd>{{currentLevel}}</dd>
            <dt>Flagged ready at</dt>
            <dd>{{readyAt}}</dd>
          </dl>
        </div>

        <p>
          The learner record holds the evidence that drove the decision —
          scenario completions, average scores, skill-domain coverage, teaching
          modes used in recent sessions, and time at the current level.
        </p>

        <p>
          <a href="{{dashboardUrl}}" class="button">Open learner record</a>
        </p>

        <p class="footnote">
          You will not receive another email about
          <strong>{{learnerName}}</strong>
          at this level for seven days. If they progress (or are demoted) to a
          different level, a fresh notification will fire as soon as they meet
          the criteria there.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="footer">
        © {{currentYear}} Amber Training. Automated message — please do not
        reply directly.
      </div>
    </div>
  </body>
</html>
